language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ aircraft_assignment: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ This problem involves assigning multiple types of aircraft to a set of routes to minimize the total operational cost. Each aircraft type has a limited number of available units. Each route has a specific passenger demand that must be satisfied. For each aircraft type and route, we are given the passenger capacity and the operational cost. The goal is to determine how many aircraft of each type to assign to each route to meet all passenger demands, stay within the availability limits for each aircraft type, and minimize the overall cost.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `aircraft_assignment.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/aircraft_assignment.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `aircraft_assignment_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py aircraft_assignment.json
$   savilerow model.eprime aircraft_assignment_1.param -run-solver

$ the number of aircraft types, derived from the data: the number of rows of capabilities (not a field of the reader's JSON)
given capabilities_dim1 : int(1..)
$ the number of routes, derived from the data: the number of columns of capabilities
given capabilities_dim2 : int(1..)
letting types = capabilities_dim1
letting routes = capabilities_dim2
$ availability[i]: the number of aircraft of type i that can be used, indices 1-based
given availability : matrix indexed by [int(1..types)] of int(0..)
$ demand[j]: the passenger demand of route j, indices 1-based
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..routes)] of int(0..)
$ capabilities[i,j]: the passenger capacity of one aircraft of type i on route j, indices 1-based
given capabilities : matrix indexed by [int(1..types), int(1..routes)] of int(0..)
$ costs[i,j]: the operational cost of one aircraft of type i on route j, indices 1-based
given costs : matrix indexed by [int(1..types), int(1..routes)] of int(0..)

$ allocation[i,j]: the number of aircraft of type i assigned to route j, indices 1-based
find allocation : matrix indexed by [int(1..types), int(1..routes)] of int(0..sum(availability))

$ the total operational cost of all assignments
minimising (sum i : int(1..types) . (sum j : int(1..routes) . costs[i,j] * allocation[i,j]))

such that
$ each route receives at least its passenger demand in seats from all the aircraft assigned to it
forAll j : int(1..routes) . (sum i : int(1..types) . capabilities[i,j] * allocation[i,j]) >= demand[j],
$ each aircraft type is assigned at most its available number of aircraft, over all routes
forAll i : int(1..types) . (sum j : int(1..routes) . allocation[i,j]) <= availability[i]
